  "Question": "If for any three distinct numbers \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) and \\(c\\) we define \\[ \\boxed{a,b,c}=\\frac{c+a}{c-b}, \\] then \\(\\boxed{1,-2,-3}=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\frac25\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\frac14\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac25\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Use the entries in their given order: \\(a=1\\), \\(b=-2\\), and \\(c=-3\\). The denominator is \\(-3-(-2)=-1\\), which is nonzero, so\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,-2,-3}\n=\\frac{-3+1}{-3-(-2)}\n=\\frac{-2}{-1}\n=2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
